---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MediaPlaceholder from '../../components/MediaPlaceholder.astro';
---
<Layout title="Meet Aya">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container hero hero--split">
      <div>
        <h1>Meet Aya</h1>
        <p>Aya brings a lot of energy into a room. She is curious, expressive and often ready to act before everyone else has finished thinking. That can lead to fun, surprises—and sometimes situations she has to work through.</p>
      </div>
      <img
        src="/images/characters/aya-meet-scene.jpg"
        alt="Aya, laughing and pointing ahead while riding a jumping sheep over a fence"
        class="character-portrait"
        width="700"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .character-portrait {
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: top center;
      border-radius: var(--radius-card);
      background: var(--brand-soft);
    }
  </style>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What makes Aya, Aya?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>She gets excited quickly.</li>
        <li>She cares deeply about the people and things she loves.</li>
        <li>She can be impatient when something feels too slow.</li>
        <li>She is willing to explore, ask and try.</li>
        <li>Her confidence does not mean she always gets things right.</li>
      </ul>
      <!-- No real approved Aya expression crops exist yet — hide this row
           rather than show generic gradient placeholders (see
           docs/OWNER_DECISIONS.md). -->
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container hero hero--split">
      <MediaPlaceholder label="SCENE — Aya and Sura sibling scene" ratio="wide" variant={2} />
      <div>
        <h2>Aya and Sura</h2>
        <p>Aya's energy and Sura's more thoughtful approach do not always match, which is exactly why they make a useful pair. Their relationship gives stories room to show children that siblings can disagree, learn from each other and still remain close.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Find Aya in</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Cards &amp; Games</h3>
          <p class="muted">Aya appears throughout the current Aya &amp; Sura flashcard decks.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/cards/">Explore Cards &amp; Games</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Giving Thanks to Allah</h3>
          <p class="muted">Aya is part of the family story in our upcoming book, nearing completion.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/books/giving-thanks-to-allah/">See the Book</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Adventure Club</h3>
          <p class="muted">Aya is one of the anchors of every monthly Club adventure.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/adventure-club/">See the Adventure Club</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
